482	     * the lower-case hex SHA-256 digest of {@code '<normalizedTelephone>|<lowerEmail>|<soundex(lastName)>'}.
483	     * The telephone is the stored E.164 value, the email its stored lower-cased form (empty when the
484	     * owner has none), and the final segment the American Soundex code of the owner's last name. Two
485	     * owners are duplicates only when their whole identity keys are equal; because the telephone is
486	     * part of the key, two owners with the same last name and postcode but different telephones have
487	     * different identity keys and are not hard duplicates.
